# Negative controls for rule J12, minted 2026-09-02.
#
# The first control is the point of the exercise: it puts the real stale sentence back
# into J10's register row, in BOTH places the row is stored, because two agreeing copies
# is exactly what made the defect invisible. A rule that only caught a disagreement
# between the copies would be green on it.
#
# Each control reverts by copying back a backup AND touching the file. shutil.copy2
# preserves the original timestamp, so a restored source looks older than the assembly
# built from the injected one and MSBuild skips the rebuild - which silently ran the
# fourth control, a markdown-only edit, against the third control's assembly. These
# verdicts are from a re-run with that fixed.

==============================================================================
J12-the-original-defect-restored
  what:  The sentence that was actually there, put back in BOTH stores. This is the defect J12 was minted for, and the register's own row-equality test is green on it.
  files: src/tests/Broiler.VM.Architecture.Tests/AssuranceRegisterRows.cs, src/tests/Broiler.VM.Architecture.Tests/rules.register.json
  suite: FAILED
  J12 said:
      the register row for J10 counts Forty-four units against the falsification-criterion requirement, and a figure a human typed goes stale where a citation cannot: "Forty-four units are assessed"
      the register row for J10 counts three units against the falsification-criterion requirement, and a figure a human typed goes stale where a citation cannot: "three of them carry"
      the register row for J10 says falsification criteria are outstanding, and the generated report states 'Required and missing | 0'
==============================================================================
